In this example, the value of 'remainder' will be 1 because 10 divided by 3 is 3 with a remainder of 1.",medium,web:Examveda.com https://www.examveda.com/c-program/practice-mcq-question-on-c-fundamentals/,
Programming in C,c fundamentals,What is the default return type of a function in C if not specified?,int,void,char,float,A,"The default return type of a function in C if not specified is Option A: int. In C, if you don't explicitly specify the return type of a function, it is assumed to return an integer (int) by default. 

So, the correct answer is: 
Option A: int 

For example, if you have a function like this: 

