In this example, the code within the if statement will be executed only if both 'x' and 'y' are true.",medium,web:Examveda.com https://www.examveda.com/c-program/practice-mcq-question-on-c-fundamentals/,
Programming in C,c fundamentals,What is the purpose of the 'sizeof' operator in C?,Calculate square root,Determine size,Perform division,Convert to string,B,"The purpose of the 'sizeof' operator in C is to determine the size of a data type or a variable in bytes. It is used to find out how much memory is allocated to a specific data type or an object in memory. 

So, the correct answer is: 
